From: SK-18 open firmware <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: u_serial: queue 1024 packets instead of 16

On the Allwinner T113 (sunxi musb, PIO) a host that writes a 58 KB frame
sends about 114 back-to-back 512-byte packets. u_serial queues only 16
receive requests of one packet each, so the queue runs dry inside every
burst. The controller driver then has a packet pending in its FIFO with
no request to put it in and its interrupt already consumed, and packets
go missing (whole 512-byte blocks) or the endpoint stalls until something
queues a request again. Queueing 1024 packets (512 KB per port, more than the largest frame the
host sends) keeps the
queue from running dry during a burst.

---
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_serial.c
@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@
  * next layer of buffering.  For TX that's a circular buffer; for RX
  * consider it a NOP.  A third layer is provided by the TTY code.
  */
-#define QUEUE_SIZE		16
+#define QUEUE_SIZE		1024
 #define WRITE_BUF_SIZE		8192		/* TX only */
 #define GS_CONSOLE_BUF_SIZE	8192
 
